From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] interconnect: qcom: sm8750: stop voting ACV like the vendor kernel

Upstream gives the SM8750 ACV BCM an enable_mask of BIT(0), so the
application processor sets that bit whenever anything votes DDR
bandwidth, including in the RPMh wake set. The SM8750 vendor kernel
never does: its ACV BCM is a mask-type BCM with no enable_mask for any
voter (HLOS, display, camera, PCIe), and HLOS only sets the perf-mode
bit (0x2) on explicit perf-mode requests.

On the AYN Odin 3 the SoC hangs in s2idle once DDR is allowed to
collapse. ACV is the only DDR-related vote that differs from the vendor
kernel: upstream's wake set raises ACV bit 0 as DDR comes back, which
the vendor never does. Match the vendor: keep ACV a mask-type
BCM so it is still committed, but with no enable bits, so Linux always
votes 0. No upstream client uses perf mode, so the perf-mode bit is
not carried over.

Add QCOM_ICC_BCM_TYPE_MASK so a BCM can use one-hot aggregation without
an enable_mask; bcm_aggregate() would otherwise send it bandwidth.
---
diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c
index a2d437a05..9d74352fb 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/bcm-voter.c
@@ -286,7 +286,7 @@ int qcom_icc_bcm_voter_commit(struct bcm_voter *voter)
 
 	mutex_lock(&voter->lock);
 	list_for_each_entry(bcm, &voter->commit_list, list) {
-		if (bcm->enable_mask)
+		if (bcm->enable_mask || bcm->type == QCOM_ICC_BCM_TYPE_MASK)
 			bcm_aggregate_mask(bcm);
 		else
 			bcm_aggregate(bcm);
diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h
index 09d879140..03b55be2a 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/icc-rpmh.h
@@ -13,6 +13,9 @@
 #define to_qcom_provider(_provider) \
 	container_of(_provider, struct qcom_icc_provider, provider)
 
+/* BCM type that always votes its enable_mask, even an empty one */
+#define QCOM_ICC_BCM_TYPE_MASK	1
+
 /**
  * struct qcom_icc_provider - Qualcomm specific interconnect provider
  * @provider: generic interconnect provider
@@ -110,7 +113,7 @@ struct qcom_icc_node {
  * struct qcom_icc_bcm - Qualcomm specific hardware accelerator nodes
  * known as Bus Clock Manager (BCM)
  * @name: the bcm node name used to fetch BCM data from command db
- * @type: latency or bandwidth bcm
+ * @type: 0, or QCOM_ICC_BCM_TYPE_MASK for a one-hot BCM without an enable_mask
  * @addr: address offsets used when voting to RPMH
  * @vote_x: aggregated threshold values, represents sum_bw when @type is bw bcm
  * @vote_y: aggregated threshold values, represents peak_bw when @type is bw bcm
diff --git a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c
index 1486c0b8f..12cf898cb 100644
--- a/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c
+++ b/drivers/interconnect/qcom/sm8750.c
@@ -1023,7 +1023,7 @@ static struct qcom_icc_node qns_gemnoc_sf = {
 
 static struct qcom_icc_bcm bcm_acv = {
 	.name = "ACV",
-	.enable_mask = BIT(0),
+	.type = QCOM_ICC_BCM_TYPE_MASK,
 	.num_nodes = 1,
 	.nodes = { &ebi },
 };
